        ->  first_fruits_basket_commanded [status]  the first fruits in a basket commanded — the STATUS the line first_fruits_declared writes on Israel: 'you shall take OF THE FIRST OF ALL THE FRUIT OF THE GROUND which you bring from your land … and put it in a basket and go to the place which the LORD your God chooses' (26:2) — 'of the first' and not all the first, the species by the two loaves' analogy (I2 — the Sifrei 297:4-5): only the seven, not dates of the hills nor fruit of the valleys nor olives not choice, not before Shavuot (Mishnah Bikkurim 1:3 — the_species a PARAMETER; Terumot 11:3 no liquids but from olives and grapes); 'your land' — the one who plants in his own and bends into another's does not bring (Bikkurim 1:1-2 in the spine's own Hebrew — the_bringers_and_the_reciters); the basket a vessel, the rich in silver and gold, the poor in peeled willow — the baskets and the first fruits to the priests (Bikkurim 3:8 — the_baskets); first-ness Exodus 23:19's (calendar.first_fruits by CALL), the grant to the priest Numbers 18:13's (korach.the_gifts by CALL); the first fruits among the five things without measure (Peah 1:1)
        ->  first_fruits_declaration_commanded [status]  the first fruits' declaration commanded — the STATUS the line first_fruits_declared writes on Israel: 'and you shall come to the priest who is in those days and say to him: I DECLARE THIS DAY TO THE LORD YOUR GOD that I have come into the land which the LORD swore to our fathers to give us' (26:3) — no ingratitude, ONCE A YEAR (the Sifrei 299:1-4); robbed, rotted, stolen, lost or unclean — he brings others in their place and does not recite, no fifth (Mishnah Bikkurim 1:8 — the_replacement a PARAMETER); the convert brings and does not recite 'which the LORD swore to OUR FATHERS' unless his mother is an Israelite; the guardian, the agent, the slave, the woman, the one of doubtful sex bring and do not recite 'which YOU have given ME' (Bikkurim 1:4-5 — the two arms); FROM SHAVUOT TO THE FEAST BRINGS AND RECITES, FROM THE FEAST TO CHANUKAH BRINGS AND DOES NOT RECITE, R. Judah ben Betera recites (Bikkurim 1:6 — the_first_fruits_window a PARAMETER and a CALENDAR DATUM on the keys atzeret and sukkot_1); the seven species, the mountains' fruit, the valleys' dates, oil-olives, beyond the Jordan — R. Yose the Galilean not from beyond the Jordan (Bikkurim 1:10)
        ->  first_fruits_recital_commanded [status]  the first fruits' recital commanded — the STATUS the line first_fruits_declared writes on Israel: 'and you shall ANSWER AND SAY BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD: a wandering Aramean was my father, and he went down to Egypt and sojourned there few in number, and he became there a nation great, mighty and many; and the Egyptians dealt ill with us and afflicted us and laid hard bondage on us; and we cried to the LORD … and the LORD brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand and an outstretched arm … and He brought us to this place and gave us this land, a land flowing with milk and honey; and now behold I have brought the first of the fruit of the ground' (26:5-10) — the priest takes the basket and WAVES (the Sifrei 300:2 — Bikkurim 2:4's waving, 'from your hand' with the owner's hand beneath); the recital IN THE HOLY TONGUE by 27:14's analogy (301:1 — Mishnah Sotah 7:2, the_tongue a PARAMETER; naso.blessing by CALL); 'Laban the Aramean sought to destroy my father' (301:3 — Onkelos at 26:5); the Haggadah's rows 301:8-24 the recital's own commentary — the seventy (joseph by CALL), the bondage (exodus_story — enslaved TWO the tape's), the cry (chukat — 26:7's clause in the Edom letter; cry_heard the tape's), the ten plagues by pairs (plague_struck THIRTEEN), milk and honey the five nations' land (Exodus 3:8, 13:5): THE RECITAL A RETELLING of the tape's own story — the readback's reference rows against the tape's lines, never a second act; the prompting of all who recite a DATA row (Bikkurim 3:7)
        ->  first_fruits_set_before_altar_commanded [status]  the first fruits set before the altar commanded — the STATUS the line first_fruits_declared writes on Israel: 'and the priest shall take the basket from your hand AND SET IT DOWN BEFORE THE ALTAR OF THE LORD YOUR GOD' (26:4), 'and you shall set it down before the LORD your God and bow down before the LORD your God' (26:10) — THE TWO SETTINGS (the Sifrei 301:31 — Bikkurim 3:1 the fig that ripened tied with a reed, 'these are first fruits'; R. Shimon's second designation after plucking — the_setting_aside a PARAMETER with both arms); acquired attached, the whole field, responsible, requiring a sacrifice, a song, waving and lodging (Bikkurim 2:4); NO ALTAR, NO FIRST FRUITS — the_temple_condition the daemon's own guard (Tosefta Shekalim 3:24; Bikkurim 1:8's scattering in the court); the flute, King Agrippas with the basket on his shoulder, the Levites' song (Bikkurim 3:4 — a DATA row of the rite's history); Shiloh and the eternal House by CALL to the place's eras (place_name.the_place_chosen)
